FAITHFUL-PARITY NOTE (states)
  The web BatteryDelta is a PURE presentational atom: props → <span>, its only hook is useTranslation
  (the i18n facade). It has exactly TWO render branches —
    • !hasData (startPct/endPct null or non-finite) → muted "—" + aria "Battery delta unknown".
    • populated → delta: compact "—"|"+N%"|"−N%" (U+2212 drop sign) or pair "A% → B%", emerald on a
      rise / amber on a drop / muted on zero; aria "Battery {from}% to {to}%".
  There is NO fetch, no React-Query cache, no Promise — therefore NO loading / error / stale / offline
  branch (nothing to load, fail, go stale, or lose connectivity to). Inventing such chrome would
  fabricate states the source does not have and contradict the web spec, so this surface reproduces
  ONLY the source's real branches — exactly as the sibling presentational primitives TimeMarker (0074)
  and ChartTimeRangeContext (0069) did, and consistent with the team's existing port of THIS component
  (feature-views ChargingBatteryDeltaDisplay: same +/U+2212 signs, — dash, emerald/amber/muted tones).

